--- b1 medium.en: A couple sells the house they bought for $140,000. The buyer pays $900,000. It is easy to assume that after 65, that profit is simply tax-free. It is not. The IRS allows a big exclusion, but part of this couple's profit is still taxed, and it can also raise their Medicare bill two years later. Here are the exact numbers from the official rules.
