--- b4 medium.en: Number one is who qualifies, and the IRS lets you exclude up to $250,000 of profit when you sell your main home, or up to $500,000 if you are married and file a joint return. To get it, you must pass two tests. You owned the home for at least 24 months, and you lived in it as your main home for at least 24 months, all within the five years before the sale.
