--- b5 medium.en: Some details matter. The 24 months do not have to be in a row. They only have to add up to 730 days. Only one spouse has to pass the ownership test, but both must pass the living in it test. You can use the exclusion once every two years and only on your main home. And if you cannot care for yourself, time in a licensed nursing home can count as time living there if the home was your main home for at least 12 months in the last five years.
   DIFF replace copione: twenty four | sentito: 24
   DIFF replace copione: seven hundred thirty | sentito: 730
   DIFF replace copione: twelve | sentito: 12
