--- b8 medium.en: Now the math for Ray and Donna. Their basis is the $140,000 they paid plus $60,000 in improvements, so $200,000. They sell at $900,000 and pay $54,000 in selling costs, so the amount realized is $846,000. Subtract the basis, and their gain is $646,000. Their exclusion is $500,000, so $146,000 is taxable.
