--- b10 medium.en: The federal tax on that gain depends on how long they owned the home. It was more than a year, so it is a long-term capital gain, taxed at 0, 15, or 20 percent. For 2026, a joint return pays 0 percent up to $98,900 of taxable income and 15 percent up to $613,700. So Ray and Donna owe it most about 21,900 dollars, and less if part falls in the zero bracket.
