--- b15 medium.en: The same gain can also touch your Social Security. The IRS says your benefits become taxable when half of your benefits plus your other income is above a base amount, 25,000 for a single filer or 32,000 on a joint return. Above 34,000 or 44,000 on a joint return, up to 85% of your benefits can be taxable. A big gain can push you higher in the year of the sale.
