--- b17 medium.en: Second, the surviving spouse. Suppose Ray passes away and Donna decides to sell. If she sells within two years of his death and is not remarried, she can still use the $500,000 exclusion as long as the other tests are met and she can count the time Ray owned and lived in the home. After the two years, the limit falls back to the single amount, $250,000. so for a widow or widower the date on the calendar matters.
